{
    "title": "Line Drawing: No Lift Puzzle",
    "description": "Draw single line is a simple puzzle game in which you are required to completely draw the given image using one finger only\ud83e\udd13\u261d\ufe0f.\r\n\r\n\ud83e\uddd0Rules of line drawing: no lift puzzle game:\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udd8c\ufe0fSingle Stroke: You must complete the drawing in one continuous motion. Lifting your finger or retracing a line is not allowed.\r\n\ud83d\udeabNo Overlaps: Lines cannot cross or overlap each other. Every element must be connected without breaking the line.\r\n\u2705Complete the Image: Every element of the image must be connected by your single line.\r\n\r\nBegin by tracing a line from the starting point. Be mindful of the path you choose, as there might be tricky sections. Visualize the entire drawing in your mind before starting. This will help you avoid dead ends or mistakes. If you find yourself stuck, try different paths or angles. Sometimes, a small adjustment can make a big difference.\r\n\r\nThe game offers a variety of puzzles, ranging from simple to extremely complex. As you progress, the challenges will become more demanding, testing your skills and problem-solving abilities. \r\n\r\n\ud83d\ude0eAre you ready to put your virtual drawing skills to the test? Give Line Puzzle Drawing No Lift Game a try and see if you can master the art of the single-stroke puzzle!",
    "descriptionHTML": "Draw single line is a simple puzzle game in which you are required to completely draw the given image using one finger only\ud83e\udd13\u261d\ufe0f.<br><br>\ud83e\uddd0Rules of line drawing: no lift puzzle game:<br><br>\ud83d\udd8c\ufe0fSingle Stroke: You must complete the drawing in one continuous motion. Lifting your finger or retracing a line is not allowed.<br>\ud83d\udeabNo Overlaps: Lines cannot cross or overlap each other. Every element must be connected without breaking the line.<br>\u2705Complete the Image: Every element of the image must be connected by your single line.<br><br>Begin by tracing a line from the starting point. Be mindful of the path you choose, as there might be tricky sections. Visualize the entire drawing in your mind before starting. This will help you avoid dead ends or mistakes. If you find yourself stuck, try different paths or angles. Sometimes, a small adjustment can make a big difference.<br><br>The game offers a variety of puzzles, ranging from simple to extremely complex. As you progress, the challenges will become more demanding, testing your skills and problem-solving abilities. <br><br>\ud83d\ude0eAre you ready to put your virtual drawing skills to the test? Give Line Puzzle Drawing No Lift Game a try and see if you can master the art of the single-stroke puzzle!",
